We are urgently looking for a REMOTE Senior QA/Mobile testing Specialist for an international organization in New York. Candidates need to be fluent in English. This position is open for freelancers and employees.
Candidates need to be able to work 2-3 hours per day in the normal office hours of New York, US. (Example 9 AM NY time equals 7:30 PM.)
QA Specialist with a background in agile software development and strong expertise in functional end-to-end testing, test automation, manual/automated testing for mobile web applications. Candidates must have experience working with MEAN platform teams building large consumer-facing web applications from the ground up.
Tasks and responsibilities:

• Create test automation frameworks from the ground up using Selenium WebDriver in several simultaneous projects;

• Responsible for developing, modifying, and executing test scripts and analyzing bugs;

• Perform manual testing on a variety of browsers and operating systems;

• Run various tests on new software products to ensure that applications satisfy all specifications and requirements;

• Record all defect details, creating and distributing reports outlining the types of defects found and the steps taken to resolve these issues and update the regression test framework;

• Automate API testing using Postman and similar tools;

• Work closely with developers to recognize the potential for any operational issues, assess risks, and resolve issues proactively;

• Maintain knowledgebase documentation in SharePoint;

Profile:

• 5+ years of experience in Quality Assurance for complex web application platforms;

• Experience with Appium, Selendroid, Robotium, or other tools for Mobile Web Application testing;

• Experience with test automation using Selenium and the ability to write scripts;

• Experience with integration testing, end-to-end testing, and load testing;

• Experience in identifying, analyzing, documenting, and reporting test results;

• Exposure to AWS, GitLab, and CI/CD pipelines;

• Exposure to testing multilingual applications;

• Good interpersonal skills to work with developers in an agile environment;

• Experience in MS Teams and SharePoint documentation is a plus;

• English language proficiency (oral and written);

Offered:

• A challenging role for an international organization in New York;

• Attractive salary package;

Interested:

If you have the determination for a rewarding career, please send your CV to us call us on +94 114312515 for more information.

